<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung issues $300 mln bonds in London.</title>
<headline>Samsung issues $300 mln bonds in London.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Electronics Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Samsung Group, said on Saturday it issued $300 million in convertible bonds in London on June 19.</p>
<p>A Samsung spokesman said the proceeds would be used to help finance the company's plan to expand facilities for 64-megabit dynamic random access memory (DRAM) chips.</p>
<p>The bond issue was arranged by Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and Samsung Securities Co Ltd.</p>
